    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="1019" n="825" xml:id="pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/7–3045</note>
                <head>No. 887<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the United States
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d887-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-30">July 30, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Political Principles for
                        Germany</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">U. S. Revision of Soviet
                        Proposal</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d887-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Soviet Delegation propose that the following addition be made to Article 8
                    paragraph IV of the “Political principles for Germany”:<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d887-f3"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Assistance, however, will be rendered to the establishment of a central
                            German Administration composed of secretaries for respective branches of
                            administration, in the first instance—of central administrative
                            institutions for foreign trade, industry, finance, transport and
                            communications. The Central German Administration shall act under the
                            direction of the Control Council.[”]</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d887-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d887-f1-content">
                <p>Attachment 10 to the summary of the Tenth Meeting of the Foreign Ministers, July
                    30. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg493">pp. 493</ref>,
